# 1. Coding Conventions

## 1.1 Language and Runtime

| Item | Standard |
|---|---|
| Python version | 3.11+ (use `match/case`, `tomllib`, `ExceptionGroup` where appropriate) |
| Type annotations | Mandatory on all public and private methods, all class attributes, all module-level variables |
| Type checker | `mypy --strict` must pass with zero errors |
| Formatter | `ruff format` (default line length 99) |
| Linter | `ruff check` with all default rules enabled |

## 1.2 Naming Conventions

| Element | Convention | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Module files | `snake_case.py` | `clipboard_manager.py` |
| Classes | `PascalCase` | `ClipboardManager` |
| Public methods | `snake_case` | `add_entry()` |
| Private methods | `_snake_case` (single underscore) | `_schedule_save()` |
| Constants | `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE` | `MAX_WORKSPACE_NAME_LENGTH` |
| Enums | `PascalCase` class, `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE` members | `TypingState.TYPING` |
| Signals | `snake_case` (descriptive verb phrase) | `entry_added`, `typing_paused` |
| Pydantic models | `PascalCase` (noun) | `ClipboardEntry`, `AppSettings` |
| Test files | `test_<module_name>.py` | `test_clipboard_manager.py` |
| Test functions | `test_<behavior>_<condition>_<expected>` | `test_add_entry_with_empty_text_raises_validation_error` |

## 1.3 Docstrings

All public classes and methods must have Google-style docstrings:

```python
def add_entry(self, text: str, source_url: str = "", source_title: str = "") -> ClipboardEntry:
    """Add a new text entry to the clipboard.

    Creates a ClipboardEntry with a generated UUID, timestamps the current time,
    computes char_count, persists to the store, and emits entry_added signal.

    Args:
        text: The clipboard text content. Must not be empty.
        source_url: The browser URL at copy time. Empty string if unavailable.
        source_title: The page title at copy time. Empty string if unavailable.

    Returns:
        The newly created ClipboardEntry with all fields populated.

    Raises:
        ValidationError: If text is empty or exceeds MAX_ENTRY_TEXT_LENGTH.
        ClipboardStorageError: If the database write fails after retry.
    """
```

## 1.4 Import Ordering

Enforced by `ruff` rule `I001`:

```python
# 1. stdlib
import sqlite3
from pathlib import Path

# 2. third-party
from loguru import logger
from pydantic import BaseModel, Field
from PySide6.QtCore import QObject, Signal

# 3. local (absolute imports only — no relative imports)
from src.models.clipboard_entry import ClipboardEntry
from src.core.events import AppSignals
```

## 1.5 File Size Limits

| Limit | Value | Action if Exceeded |
|---|---|---|
| Max lines per file | 400 | Split into submodules |
| Max methods per class | 20 | Extract helper class |
| Max parameters per method | 6 | Introduce parameter object (Pydantic model) |
| Max cyclomatic complexity | 10 | Refactor into smaller functions |

