# 10. Thread Ownership Matrix

| Class | Owner Thread | Rationale |
|---|---|---|
| `BatmanOverlayApp` | Main | QApplication runs on main thread |
| `MainWindow` | Main | All Qt widgets are main-thread only |
| `TitleBar`, `Sidebar`, `StatusBar` | Main | Qt widgets |
| `ClipboardWidget`, `TypingWidget`, `SettingsPanel` | Main | Qt widgets |
| `SearchDialog`, `ToastWidget` | Main | Qt widgets |
| `SplashScreen` | Main | Qt widget |
| `ConfigManager` | Main | Reads/writes config; emits signals |
| `SessionManager` | Main | Timer-driven; delegates heavy I/O to QThreadPool |
| `WorkspaceManager` | Main | Orchestrates workspace switch on main thread |
| `HotkeyManager` | Main | Processes WM_HOTKEY on main thread event loop |
| `SearchEngine` | Main | Delegates FTS5 queries; results returned on main |
| `NotificationManager` | Main | UI routing |
| `ThemeManager` | Main | QSS application must be main thread |
| `AccessibilityManager` | Main | QAccessible is main-thread only |
| `UpdateManager` | Main (dispatch) | Actual HTTPS request on QThreadPool |
| `PerformanceMonitor` | Main (sampling via QTimer) | Metrics sampled periodically |
| `TabManager` | Main | Manages Qt widgets |
| `NavigationManager` | Main | Forwards commands to QWebEngineView |
| `BrowserWidget` | Main | QWebEngineView must be main-thread |
| `BrowserProfileManager` | Main | QWebEngineProfile is main-thread |
| `ClipboardManager` | Main | Business logic; delegates heavy DB ops to QThreadPool |
| `ClipboardStore` | Main (primary), QThreadPool (bulk ops) | Thread-local DB connections |
| `TypingEngine` | Main (control), _TypingWorker (execution) | Commands on main; keystrokes on worker |
| `_TypingWorker` | **Dedicated QThread** | SendInput calls with sleep delays |
| `TypingQueue` | Main | Queue management on main thread |
| `SpeedController` | **Dedicated QThread** (read) + Main (write) | Read by worker; speed set by main |
| `DatabaseManager` | Thread-local connections | Each thread opens its own connection |
| `JsonStore` | Any (stateless) | Atomic file I/O is inherently thread-safe |
| `MigrationRunner` | Main (during boot) | Migrations run once before UI |
| `InputSimulator` | **Dedicated QThread** (via _TypingWorker) | SendInput calls |
| `HotkeyRegistry` | Main | RegisterHotKey must be called from the thread that owns the message loop |

