# 11. State Machines and Lifecycle Diagrams

## 11.1 Typing Engine State Machine

### States

| State | Description | Entry Action | Exit Action |
|---|---|---|---|
| `IDLE` | No typing job active | Clear `_current_job` | — |
| `COUNTDOWN` | Pre-typing delay (3, 2, 1...) | Emit `countdown_tick(3)` | — |
| `TYPING` | Characters being sent via SendInput | Emit `typing_started` or `typing_resumed` | — |
| `PAUSED` | Typing suspended by user | Emit `typing_paused`; set pause event | — |
| `COMPLETED` | All characters sent | Emit `typing_completed` | Worker thread exits |
| `CANCELLED` | User cancelled during typing or pause | Emit `typing_cancelled` | Worker thread exits |
| `ERROR` | SendInput failure or worker crash | Emit `typing_error` | Worker thread exits |

### Transition Table

| Current State | Trigger | Guard | Next State | Side Effect |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `IDLE` | `start(job)` called | Job text is not empty | `COUNTDOWN` | Create worker thread; start countdown timer |
| `IDLE` | `pause()` called | — | `IDLE` | No-op (idempotent) |
| `IDLE` | `resume()` called | — | `IDLE` | No-op (idempotent) |
| `IDLE` | `cancel()` called | — | `IDLE` | No-op (idempotent) |
| `COUNTDOWN` | Timer tick | seconds > 0 | `COUNTDOWN` | Emit `countdown_tick(seconds - 1)` |
| `COUNTDOWN` | Timer tick | seconds == 0 | `TYPING` | Start character loop on worker thread |
| `COUNTDOWN` | `cancel()` called | — | `CANCELLED` | Stop timer; destroy worker |
| `COUNTDOWN` | `pause()` called | — | `PAUSED` | Stop countdown timer; save remaining seconds |
| `TYPING` | Character sent | chars_done < chars_total | `TYPING` | Emit `typing_progress(chars_done, chars_total)` |
| `TYPING` | Character sent | chars_done == chars_total | `COMPLETED` | Emit `typing_completed` |
| `TYPING` | `pause()` called | — | `PAUSED` | Set pause event; worker blocks on event |
| `TYPING` | `cancel()` called | — | `CANCELLED` | Set cancel flag; worker exits loop |
| `TYPING` | SendInput error | — | `ERROR` | Emit `typing_error`; worker exits |
| `PAUSED` | `resume()` called | — | `TYPING` / `COUNTDOWN` | Clear pause event; resume from saved position |
| `PAUSED` | `cancel()` called | — | `CANCELLED` | Destroy worker |
| `COMPLETED` | — | — | (terminal) | Auto-dequeue next job from TypingQueue |
| `CANCELLED` | — | — | (terminal) | Set state to IDLE after cleanup |
| `ERROR` | — | — | (terminal) | Set state to IDLE after cleanup |

### Invalid Transitions (Must Log WARNING and No-Op)

- `start()` when state is not `IDLE`
- `resume()` when state is not `PAUSED`
- Any command on terminal states (`COMPLETED`, `CANCELLED`, `ERROR`)

## 11.2 Application Lifecycle

```
main(argv)
    │
    ├── Parse args (--version → exit)
    ├── Create BatmanOverlayApp(argv)
    │
    ▼
boot()
